within ThermoSysPro.MultiFluids;

package Machines "Machines"
  extends ThermoSysPro.UsersGuide.Documentation.ThermoSysProPackageIcon;
  annotation(Documentation(info = "## Copyright © EDF 2002 - 2025

## ThermoSysPro Version 4.2

Machines  


The multifluids machines modeled are CHP (Combined Heat and Power) as well as internal combustion engines.  
The internal combustion engine (or alternating engine) is a classical motor, using fuel to produce mechanical energy.   
The CHP engine functions similarly but is more efficient, as the heat produced by the fuel combustion is reused.  

For a better understanding of the underlying physics, see Chap. 15 of :cite:`el19`.  



     

    "));
end Machines;